# The Construct — Vite environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored). With no file at all the game boots and asks
# which app it is; `npm run setup` creates one and prints the id. Players then
# sign in THROUGH Crowded Kingdoms (hosted sign-in) and come back with a token
# for that app; this page never sees a password.
#
# DO NOT put a hostname in this file. The installed CrowdyJS dist-tag already
# carries the correct public API origin for its tier (`latest` -> production);
# a hostname written here goes stale the first time the fleet moves.

# Pin the app this checkout plays (the id `npm run setup` printed). Required
# for a deployed build; the dev server can also take it from the no-app card.
# VITE_APP_ID=

# Override the API origin (root, no /graphql). Only for a private deployment or
# a local API stack; leave unset to use the SDK's baked default for its tier.
# Use `same-origin` when the dev server proxies /graphql (public-IP IDE and
# localhost Playwright then share one build).
# VITE_CROWDY_HTTP_URL=

# Hosted sign-in page. Required when VITE_CROWDY_HTTP_URL is not a CK tier host
# (a same-origin proxy or raw IP) — the SDK cannot derive Studio from those.
# VITE_AUTHORIZE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5173/authorize

# Optional Studio origin for in-game links (Wallet). Defaults to the origin of
# VITE_AUTHORIZE_URL. Set this only when Studio is on a different host than
# /authorize.
# VITE_STUDIO_URL=

# Enable/disable CLIENT-target Crowdy Studio mods in this build (default: on).
# A fork that wants SERVER-only Studio sets this to 0.
# VITE_CONSTRUCT_CLIENT_MODS=1

# App-token refresh cadence in seconds (default 1200 = 20 min; tokens live ~30).
# VITE_APP_TOKEN_REFRESH_SECONDS=1200
